cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Gravitas: an interactive astrophysics sandbox for teaching"
message: "If you use Gravitas in teaching or research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ziegler
    given-names: Carl
    affiliation: Stephen F. Austin State University
    email: Carl.Ziegler@sfasu.edu
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gravitas-sim/gravitas-sim.github.io"
url: "https://gravitas-sim.online"
abstract: >-
  Gravitas is a browser-based N-body gravity sandbox and astronomy teaching
  tool. It ships 53 configurable scenarios drawn from real and idealized
  systems, 12 guided investigations in which undergraduate students predict,
  measure and plot their own data, instructor materials with answer keys, and
  a public account of what the underlying model does and does not represent.
  It runs entirely client-side as a static site, requires no account or
  installation, and encodes any simulation state into a shareable URL.
keywords:
  - astronomy education
  - physics education
  - N-body simulation
  - orbital mechanics
  - exoplanets
  - habitable zone
  - interactive simulation
  - open educational resources
